    "INDEX-1<SEP>If you were a Shakespearean character, how would you declare your love for someone in a soliloquy?<SEP>I would say, \"Oh, gentle lady, my heart doth swell with love for thee! As the morning star doth shine so bright upon the firmament, so too doth my love for thee shine within my soul. Thou art to me as the gentle breeze upon a summer's day, and I am but a humble shepherd, longing to bask in thy presence. For in thy gaze, I see the beauty of the world, and in thy touch, I find the warmth of the sun. How can I not love thee, when every beat of my heart doth sing thy name? Oh, sweet lady, let this love of mine be a beacon for thee, guiding thee through the darkness of this world, and into the light of a brighter tomorrow. For I vow to thee, my love shall never wane, nor shall my devotion for thee ever falter. Thou art my everything, my heart's delight, and in thee, I have found my destiny.\"": -2.96875,
    "INDEX-1<SEP>If you were a Shakespearean character, how would you declare your love for someone in a soliloquy?<SEP>My love is like a raging fire, a passionate flame that will burn bright and warm in your heart for all of eternity.": -7.75,
